{"at": "2026-11-26T09:32:31Z", "class": ["software.performance"], "evidence": ["review:sha256-4af07be7050c"], "id": "00ded95a834f3c4b", "kind": "note", "scope": "family:software", "session": "dadd45b5-0351-567e-8ad3-af5dd32da40e", "signal": "first-success", "text": "When a game is slow, measure on the target machine before cutting features: a pixel line (frame time at three render scales and a tiny window) separates pixels from the rest, and replacing one material at a time with a plain one names the dear shader. Here it showed a procedural land shader was 40 % of the frame and scripts under 1 ms, the opposite of what the cloud machine suggested.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-26T09:32:31Z", "class": ["software.performance"], "evidence": ["review:sha256-b05f6d868f17"], "id": "74bd9affbe0c8381", "kind": "note", "scope": "family:software", "session": "dadd45b5-0351-567e-8ad3-af5dd32da40e", "signal": "first-success", "text": "A read-back from the GPU (viewport texture to image) stalls the main thread until the GPU has finished everything queued; baked off-screen pictures belong in a disk cache keyed by the inputs' hash, read on a worker thread, never rebuilt at each start.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-26T09:32:32Z", "class": ["operations.multi-agent"], "evidence": ["review:sha256-1cabb88738ef"], "id": "c441b7b26099c17b", "kind": "note", "scope": "global", "session": "dadd45b5-0351-567e-8ad3-af5dd32da40e", "signal": "rework", "text": "With several chats on one repository, give the integration branch one fixed name that survives every handover, and have each chat keep a small status block in its own file on its own branch that a script collects into one board: renaming the lead's branch at each handover cost a round of messages and left a chat on another machine unreachable.", "trust": "observed"}
{"at": "2026-11-26T09:32:32Z", "class": ["software.testing"], "evidence": ["review:sha256-5a7a388fd668"], "id": "781feb03d916e07f", "kind": "note", "scope": "family:software", "session": "dadd45b5-0351-567e-8ad3-af5dd32da40e", "signal": "rework", "text": "A test runner that loads every test script can hang silently when one script has a semantic error the syntax check does not catch: when a first run after adding a test takes far longer than expected, read the raw log before waiting.", "trust": "observed"}
